["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-7cd0959b3d56eeeca2062c47965a876cc9c29b0003ead4111d5747e8f69fa038","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# Direct library return observations\n\n## Accepted request and evidence\n\nThe operator approved the ER executable-contract plan on 2026-09-28, explicitly including necessary narrow ESS capability changes. ER pure APIs return values and do not publish events. ESS 0.37.0 only compares command response values through emitted event mappings. Authored `response:` is refused as ESS-AUTHOR-001, while a silent `accepts: nothing` outcome checks no returned value. A reproducer is retained in ER `ess/reproducers/pure-return/`. This work is independent of the parked ESS evolution program.\n\n## Scope\n\nExtend the existing typed command-response observation boundary with authored direct value assertions, checked against the source command response type, and automatic response shape checks where declared. Preserve old canonical bytes and readers; admit the new observation only in a new scenario/suite format. An old reader must refuse it before target callbacks. Rust runner must compare actual SemanticCommandResult.response from the exact invocation, without requiring or manufacturing an event, a persistent subject, or a query view.\n\nTyped declarations already exist: command response Field, SemanticCommandResult.response, and response::Observation; this adds observation of existing nouns, not a new runtime entity.\n\n## Acceptance scenarios\n\n- pure_return_correct_literal_passes_without_events\n- pure_return_wrong_literal_fails_named_scenario\n- pure_return_absent_field_and_extra_field_refuse\n- pure_return_unknown_response_coordinate_refuses_at_compile\n- pure_return_old_formats_refuse_before_target_effects\n- pure_return_legacy_suite_bytes_unchanged\n- pure_return_complete_nested_values_preserve_order_and_duplicates\n\nUse existing admitted suite and report/2 paths. Add a minimal design, compatibility tests, and run format, conformance crate tests and Clippy plus touched CLI checks. No Go/TypeScript runtime code is introduced: if those producers cannot execute the new construct, they must refuse generation explicitly. Binary64 remains explicitly unsupported in native ESS typed conformance pending its own governed extension; do not silently relax its admission.\n","status":"draft","title":"Assert typed direct library returns without invented events"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/direct-library-return-observations"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-125ab5cf1dd517e2220a5e10378273d9@1"],"audit":["aud-9e683df4881f7f5054ff7f8b6e778203"],"command_id":"cmd-child-7cd0959b3d56eeeca2062c47965a876cc9c29b0003ead4111d5747e8f69fa038","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-9e6840f4881f846954ff808b6e7783b6"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-7cd0959b3d56eeeca2062c47965a876cc9c29b0003ead4111d5747e8f69fa038","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-7cd0959b3d56eeeca2062c47965a876cc9c29b0003ead4111d5747e8f69fa038@1~5de8490cf5a8b362","recorded_at":"2026-09-28T01:52:36Z"},"subject":["aep.applied","child-7cd0959b3d56eeeca2062c47965a876cc9c29b0003ead4111d5747e8f69fa038"]}]